WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.400
 As educators, we want our students  

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.800
 to focus on learning, 
  not troubleshooting package installations. 

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.240
 RStudio Cloud gives us the ability 
  to install all of the packages 

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.760
 we'd like to use for a course or workshop 
  using a base project. 

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.520
 This means that all of the packages 
  we need are pre-installed 

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.520
 in all of the projects 
  within our shared workspace . 

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.880
 Let me show you how that works from 
  within our workspace. 

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.560
 We'll click on new project.  

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.080
 This will deploy a new RStudio project 
  for us. Once we have our project 

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:36.600
 we can install all of the packages 
  we'd like to use for our course. 

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.640
 You can either create an R script 
  with all of the package installations 

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.400
 or complete the installations 
  via the console. 

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.400
 One benefit to installing packages via 

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.680
 the console is that it prevents 
  a bit of confusion for your learners. 

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.000
 This is because any R scripts or files 
  that you create in your base project 

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.800
 will be available to all of the learners 
  within your workspace. 

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.840
 Therefore, it's possible that learners 
  may run the package installation script, 

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.720
 thinking that this is a necessary 
  step in the process. 

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.800
 We can name our project 
  anything that we'd like, 

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.680
 and for this example, we'll name it base 
  by clicking on Untitled Project 

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.200
 and typing in base. Before we can set this 
  as the default for our workspace 

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.600
 we need to make it accessible 
  to all of our learners 

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.280
 by clicking on the settings wheel, then 
  clicking on the access tab. And from the 

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.760
 who can view this project dropdown 
  choosing the Everyone option. 

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.600
 Once our project has been created and made 
  accessible to everyone in the workspace, 

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.680
 we can move out of the project 
  and back to the workspace 

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.080
 by clicking on the workspace 
  name in the top menu from the workspace. 

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.200
 We'll click on the settings  

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.680
 wheel on the top right. And from the base 
  RStudio project dropdown menu 

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.160
 choosing our base project. 

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.520
 This now sets up all of our  

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.240
 learners with the packages 
  we've installed, but that's not all. 

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.040
 We can also create a new base project 
  at any time with additional 

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.760
 package installations.  

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.320
 Because changes to the base 
  project are not retroactive, 

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.800
 any previous installations will be carried 
  forward, along with the updated 

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:10.120
 installations established when we create 
  and assign a new base project. 

